      "title": "9.8.4 Weak acids aur weak bases ke salts (Roman Urdu)",
      "language": "roman_ur",
      "variant_of": "C11-CHEM-CH9-9.8.4",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 205,
          "pdf_to": 205,
          "note": "Roman Urdu explanation of topic 9.8.4, printed page 205."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Weak acid aur weak base se bane salts (jaise ammonium acetate, NH₄CH₃COO) ke liye:"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Conjugate acid (NH₄⁺) aur conjugate base (CH₃COO⁻) dono pH par asar karte hain."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{NH4CH3COO_{(aq)} <=> NH4^+_{(aq)} + CH3COO^-_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "NH₄CH₃COO(aq) ⇌ NH₄⁺(aq) + CH₃COO⁻(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "NH₄⁺ hydrolyse ho kar H₃O⁺ banata hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{NH4^+_{(aq)} + H2O_{(l)} <=> NH3_{(aq)} + H3O^+_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "NH₄⁺(aq) + H₂O(l) ⇌ NH₃(aq) + H₃O⁺(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "CH₃COO⁻ hydrolyse ho kar OH⁻ banata hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3COO^-_{(aq)} + H2O_{(aq)} <=> CH3COOH_{(aq)} + OH^-_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃COO⁻(aq) + H₂O(aq) ⇌ CH₃COOH(aq) + OH⁻(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Solution ka aakhri pH is par munhasir hai ke conjugate acid aur conjugate base mein se kaun zyada taqatwar hai. Jo reaction zyada chale (dominant ho), us ke mutabiq solution acidic, basic ya taqreeban neutral hota hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Salt hydrolysis ka khulasa",
            "header": [
              "Salt kis se bana",
              "Misal",
              "Hydrolyse hone wala ion",
              "Solution"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "strong acid + strong base",
                "NaCl",
                "koi nahi",
                "neutral"
              ],
              [
                "strong acid + weak base",
                "NH₄Cl",
                "NH₄⁺ (H₃O⁺ deta hai)",
                "acidic"
              ],
              [
                "weak acid + strong base",
                "CH₃COONa",
                "CH₃COO⁻ (OH⁻ deta hai)",
                "basic"
              ],
              [
                "weak acid + weak base",
                "NH₄CH₃COO",
                "NH₄⁺ aur CH₃COO⁻ dono",
                "nisbati taqat par munhasir"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Mukhtasar khulasa"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Weak acid + weak base ka salt (NH₄CH₃COO): dono ions hydrolyse hote hain, NH₄⁺ se H₃O⁺ aur CH₃COO⁻ se OH⁻; pH dono ki nisbati taqat par munhasir hai."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
